"""Render final reports from completed immutable scalar results; no selection."""
import pathlib,json,numpy as np
R=pathlib.Path('/root/ouro-catc-sol-20261116');P=R/'phaseC'
load=lambda p:json.loads(p.read_text())
assert load(R/'STATUS.json')['pilot_complete']
B=load(R/'SUMMARY.json');A=load(P/'ADAPTATION_SUMMARY.json');F=load(P/'FULL_ANSWER_SUMMARY.json');S=load(P/'SELECTED_INFERENCE_PROFILE.json');T={n:load(P/n/'COMPLETE.json') for n in ['catc14','unstructured14','value7','routing7']}
def tbl(methods):
 t='| Method | Correct/N | Accuracy | Delta vs native K4 (pp) | Rescue/damage | Paired 95% delta (pp) |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\n'
 for n,v in methods.items():
  ci=v.get('paired_ci95',v.get('paired_vs_nativeK4',{}).get('ci95'))
  t+=f"| {n} | {v['correct']}/{v['n']} | {v['accuracy']:.3%} | {v['pp_vs_nativeK4']:+.3f} | {v['rescue']}/{v['damage']} | [{100*ci[0]:+.3f}, {100*ci[1]:+.3f}] |\n"
 return t
body=''
for dataset,z in A.items():
 body+=f'## {dataset.title()} Joint-Option\n\n'
 body+=('All 299 ARC Validation questions; previously exposed and used for checkpoint selection.\n\n' if dataset=='validation' else '997/1000 SciQ Validation questions, after three duplicate-option exclusions fixed without inspecting outcomes. No SciQ examples were used to select coefficients or checkpoints.\n\n')
 body+=tbl(z['methods'])+'\n'
body+='## Standard Full-Answer\n\nAll 299 ARC Validation questions; matched sequential teacher-forced prefixes, four recurrent passes, no KV cache, 25 full-answer demonstrations. The primary score is the FP32 sum of token log probabilities divided by the answer character count, excluding the leading space. Full token sums and token-normalized alternatives are retained. Native and LoopCD are fresh matched executions; historical batched teacher-forcing numbers are not pooled.\n\n'+tbl(F)+'\n'
body+='All confidence intervals above are descriptive, question-paired 5,000-bootstrap intervals with seed 20261116. The independent confirmatory family consists of the primary 14-scalar policy and Validation-selected structured policy, each compared with native K4, E6 conservative, and the trained unstructured control (six one-sided Bonferroni contrasts). Both policies fail this benefit gate. Other evaluation populations and score protocols are kept separate.\n'
(R/'GENERALIZATION_RESULTS.md').write_text('# Frozen evaluation and generalization\n\n'+body)
train='# Static-coefficient fitting\n\nAll Ouro parameters remained frozen. The four runs used the same projected SPSA schedule, initialized at zero: learning rate .05/(t+1)^.602; perturbation .05/(t+1)^.101; L2 penalty .01; coefficient bounds [-.25,.25]. The actual post-BF16 correction was bounded at 10% per site. Each run allowed one shuffled Train epoch (35 minibatches of up to 32; seed 20261116). Validation candidate CE was checked at steps 0/12/24/35; earliest minimum won; two consecutive non-improving checks stopped a run.\n\n| Policy | Active coefficients | Steps | Distinct Train IDs queried | Train forwards | Selected step | Validation CE |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n'
for n,v in T.items():train+=f"| {n} | {v['parameters']} | {v['steps']} | {v['training_distinct_ids']} | {v['training_forward_evaluations']} | {v['best_step']} | {v['validation_CE']:.9f} |\n"
train+='\nThe primary catc14, unstructured14 and value7 select the all-zero identity checkpoint. Routing7 selects step 12, trained on its first 384 shuffled Train examples. Later Train and Validation queries still count toward the selection cost. Exact coefficients are in phaseC/SELECTED_COEFFICIENTS.json, with every SPSA step and checkpoint row preserved.\n\nThe secondary structured family selects routing7 using Joint Validation CE before SciQ or FullAnswer outputs. This is supervised development calibration. The primary catc14 hypothesis is retained separately. No independent-set coefficient search occurred.\n\nDerivative-free fitting was chosen prospectively to avoid storing full backbone backward state within this pilot. A backpropagation out-of-memory failure was not measured, and convergence is not established. Fourteen parameters do not remove the cost of the 6,796 training forward queries or the additional Validation checks. Actual wall envelopes, physical forwards, serial deployment memory and latency are recorded separately in phaseC/COMPUTE_COSTS.json and phaseC/SELECTED_INFERENCE_PROFILE.json.\n'
(R/'FOURTEEN_PARAMETER_TRAINING.md').write_text(train)
profile='| Policy | Median seconds | Relative to native | Peak allocated GiB |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n'
for n,v in S['methods'].items():profile+=f"| {n} | {v['median_seconds']:.4f} | {v['relative_vs_native']:.3f} | {v['peak_allocated_bytes']/2**30:.3f} |\n"
(R/'BASELINE_COMPARISON.md').write_text('# Matched baselines and deployment cost\n\nAll frozen output-only rules are shown below, including fixed E6 fusion and repository LoopCD. The E6 fixed 0:1:1:2 weighted rule differs from the model-gate weighted output. The strongest Train output rule is E6 conservative (969/1094); no fixed structured row beats it. The strongest observed evaluation baseline is reported descriptively and is not used to select a new policy.\n\n'+body+'\n## Serial deployment profile\n\nThree original technical questions, one warmup and three timed repetitions per question, one full-shaped K4 head, four complete passes. All full-vocabulary endpoints must match the corresponding captured policy exactly. Zero coefficients bypass CATC instrumentation. Nonzero policies retain numerical auditing overhead.\n\n'+profile+'\nThe main Phase B capture used four readout heads for native and two for modified policies, so those capture timers are not matched deployment latency. RUNTIME_AND_MEMORY.json preserves those capture costs for exact CPU replay; the serial profiles give the matched inference comparison.\n')
review='# Final scientific review\n\n**Outcome C: no demonstrated utility gain.** The primary objective of outperforming native K4 and strong matched output-only baselines was not met.\n\nOn full Train1094, native K4 gets 966 correct. The best fixed structured row, routing +0.1, gets 969, tying E6 conservative. No structured configuration passes the predeclared accuracy/control gate. Value +0.1 and joint positive correction pass only the separate secondary gold-margin gate; that reproducible score effect authorized the small static-coefficient fit.\n\nThe selected primary 14-scalar policy is exactly native. The Validation-selected routing-only policy gets 261/299, equal to native; E6 conservative gets 263. On the independently selected SciQ997 population, native and fixed value +0.1 get 924, while routing-only gets 922. Neither primary nor secondary passes its independent benefit gate.\n\n'
review+='FullAnswer is a separate protocol: native K4 gets 157/299, fixed value +0.1 gets 162/299 (5 rescues, 0 damages; descriptive paired 95% delta [+0.334, +3.344] pp), and the Validation-selected routing-only policy gets 161/299. Matched LoopCD 1 gets 173/299. Thus the fixed correction has a protocol-specific gain over native while remaining below the strong output-only baseline; it does not establish the failed Joint-Option and independent-benchmark objective.\n\nThe evidence covers one bounded coefficient grid and one fixed SPSA configuration, not every possible CATC optimizer or information-flow controller. No additional head, layer, threshold, coefficient or Gate search was launched to rescue the result. ARC Test was not justified and was not run.\n\n## Interpretation and numerical scope\n\nThe value/routing decomposition is algebraic and non-unique, so component score effects do not establish causal attribution to accuracy. Later K2 sites use the actual trajectory after upstream edits, while K1 is natural: this is the explicitly frozen sequential feedback variant. It is not a separate unmodified K2 donor trajectory. Probabilities are FP64 reconstructions from actual post-RoPE Q/K, rather than bitwise extraction of fused SDPA internal probabilities. Original SDPA, projection, RMSNorm, residual, MLP, K3 and K4 operations remain in place.\n\nZero coefficients match full-vocabulary outputs bitwise on three fixed technical cases; all intended direct write sites and all four passes are audited. FP64-to-FP32 decomposition sensitivity on the same three cases changes 0/48 endpoint predictions and zero tie sets; that is not full-cohort or cross-hardware robustness. The exact sources, prospective freezes, numerical repairs and source-version reconstruction receipts are retained.\n\nValidation was exposed and used for selection. SciQ is independent within this study, with no claim of absence from pretraining or exclusion of every semantic overlap. Its three exclusions are duplicate options; no additional ARC overlap was found by the stated exact/Jaccard screen. SciQ attribution and CC-BY-NC 3.0 terms accompany the inputs.\n\nFull raw heads and Q/K/V witnesses remain on the server under hash manifests. Published scalar rows reproduce summaries and statistical decisions on CPU; they do not substitute for rerunning GPU forwards.\n\n'+profile
(R/'FINAL_SCIENTIFIC_REVIEW.md').write_text(review)
# Complete K2/K4 and effect groups directly from saved rows, without selecting a policy.
rows=[json.loads(l) for l in (R/'TRAINING_FREE_ALL_ROWS.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]
effect='| Setting | K2 correct | K2 rescue/damage | K4 correct | K4 rescue/damage | K4 margin positive/negative/zero |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n'
for i in range(1,7):
 n=f'T{i}_structured';v=B[n+'_K2'];w=B[n+'_K4'];d=[]
 for q in rows:
  a=q['records'][0]['scores']['4']['candidate_logits'];b=next(z for z in q['records'] if z['name']==n)['scores']['4']['candidate_logits'];g=q['gold'];gap=lambda z:z[g]-max(x for k,x in enumerate(z) if k!=g);d.append(gap(b)-gap(a))
 effect+=f"| {n} | {v['correct']} | {v['same_depth_rescue']}/{v['same_depth_damage']} | {w['correct']} | {w['same_depth_rescue']}/{w['same_depth_damage']} | {sum(x>0 for x in d)}/{sum(x<0 for x in d)}/{sum(x==0 for x in d)} |\n"
(R/'CAUSAL_ABLATIONS.md').write_text('# Component and control comparisons\n\nAll 1094 Train questions are retained, including negative and zero effects. Margins are gold logit minus the highest non-gold candidate logit; positive/negative signs below use exact saved FP32 candidate scores, with no post-hoc significance threshold. Rescue/damage is relative to the native endpoint at the same depth.\n\n'+effect+'\nEvery nonzero setting has unrelated-layer, randomized-direction, prefix-only and signed output-scaling controls. Their complete results and paired accuracy/margin contrasts are in SUMMARY.json and GATES.json. Randomization preserves requested basis norm; it does not guarantee exact equality of realized post-BF16 doses after different upstream trajectories. Actual per-site norms and clipping are retained, and all actual writebacks obey the 10% bound.\n\nThe two 30-contrast accuracy and gold-margin gate families are separate; no global 5% family-wise claim across both routes is made. None passes the accuracy gate; T1 and T5 pass only the secondary score gate.\n\n'+train)
readme='''# CATC loop-control pilot

Completed original CATC study, Outcome C: no demonstrated improvement over native K4 and strong matched output baselines. Read FINAL_SCIENTIFIC_REVIEW.md for the scientific decision and GENERALIZATION_RESULTS.md for every evaluated method.

The study contains Train1094 x 31 fixed/control configurations, four bounded scalar fitting runs, full ARC Validation299, independent SciQ997, and separately matched Standard FullAnswer Validation299. Original Ouro weights remain frozen. ARC Test was not used.

Code is in code/, fitting and frozen evaluation artifacts in phaseC/. Follow REPRODUCE.md for two CPU statistical replays. Raw full-vocabulary tensors and Q/K/V witnesses remain on the server with hash manifests. The publication contains complete per-question scalar results and compressed, losslessly sharded archives.

Schema: directly_changed_K2_R_sites uses zero-based physical layer indices and records attempted writes, which can be unchanged after quantization. Norm fields are [requested_preclip_L2, cap_L2, total_scale, actual_BF16_writeback_L2, prepatch_SDPA_L2]. Attention probabilities normalize over the full causal sequence before region slicing. Native K2 endpoints are captured during full four-pass execution; no early-exit timing benefit is claimed.

SciQ: Welbl, Liu and Gardner (2017), Crowdsourcing Multiple Choice Science Questions; AllenAI dataset, CC-BY-NC 3.0. Only the Validation split was read. Supporting paragraphs were omitted; original ARC demonstrations were retained. Dataset archive and evaluated-input hashes are recorded.
'''
(R/'README.md').write_text(readme)
print('READABLE_REPORTS_COMPLETE')
